  "reason": "All four completed experiments used concat fusion, so the effect of weighted fusion remains entirely untested. config_003 (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) is the current best at 0.629 acc, and config_022 is identical except for switching fusion from concat to weighted. This isolates a single design variable (fusion strategy) against the strongest known baseline, directly testing whether learned channel weighting improves over simple concatenation. Under a tight budget, this is the highest-information single-variable extension: if weighted fusion helps, it identifies a new lever to exploit across other encoders/aggregations; if it does not, it confirms concat is sufficient and redirects budget toward untested encoders (scvi_n200, scgpt) or image backbones (resnet50)."
}

